  "body": "## Summary\n\nConnect existing TW-RW receivers to row resolution. This is an incremental fork stack preview, not an upstream-main merge candidate.\n\n## Problem\n\nThe final shard must resolve while original splits/gradient scaling remain correct.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Install resolution on the final TW-RW receiving shard using the existing native carrier.\n- Keep existing partitioning, output maps and gradient scaling.\n- Extend the real fixture to assert resolved input and no second lookup, with parity/jagged/gradient checks.\n\n## Scope / Out of Scope\n\nTW-RW only. Additional backends/layouts belong to their separate previews. Real network PS, NVLink/GIN and a complete combination matrix are not certified here. 563 is an independent existing-main failure fix; generic service transactions are not promised.\n\n## Validation\n\nCurrent-prefix2-GPU parity/jagged and 4-GPU gradient checks pass. Local packages match current Docker tags: PyTorch 2.13/cu130, FBGEMM 1.8, TorchRec v1.8.0-rc1 on SM120. Native/JIT was freshly built from current source. Current integrated 551 reports 865/6 per rank, but each prefix keeps its own evidence. Exact tested/published heads, documentation-only successors, source hashes and all commands: [PR_VALIDATION_MATRIX.md](https://github.com/WEIXILIN0307/recsys-examples/tree/ee3e312450572772d8b73285c7fba5026efd0186/docs/issue459/current-main-20261117/PR_VALIDATION_MATRIX.md). Root pre-commit passes; direct package mypy retains baseline errors without new normalized diagnostics. No CI/full-container pass is inferred.\n\n## Performance\n\nNo blanket throughput gain. Measured main regressions remain; the separate raw compatibility slice has isolated 11\u201312.7% raw improvement. [PERFORMANCE_REPORT.md](https://github.com/WEIXILIN0307/recsys-examples/tree/ee3e312450572772d8b73285c7fba5026efd0186/docs/issue459/current-main-20261117/PERFORMANCE_REPORT.md) distinguishes measured commits, before/after controls and subsequent refusal-only changes. No isolated speedup is attributed to this prefix without its own measurement.\n\n## Dependencies / Follow-ups\n\nBase: the declared prerequisite base in the split plan. Full ownership and actual base hashes: [PR_SPLIT_PLAN.md](https://github.com/WEIXILIN0307/recsys-examples/tree/ee3e312450572772d8b73285c7fba5026efd0186/docs/issue459/current-main-20261117/PR_SPLIT_PLAN.md). Design: NVIDIA/recsys-examples#552; integration: NVIDIA/recsys-examples#551. Keep Draft pending maintainer/CI/performance/deployment gates; this does not close #459.\n",
